<title>USA: FAA proposes Boeing 777 overhead unit change.</title>
<headline>FAA proposes Boeing 777 overhead unit change.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Aviation Administration said Friday it proposed requiring replacement of passenger overhead electronics units in Boeing 777 aircraft to prevent overheating and potential fires.</p>
<p>In a notice in the Federal Register, the FAA said its action was prompted by reports of smoke coming from overhead panels near reading lights due to overheating transformers.</p>
<p>FAA said any comments on its proposal must be received by May 15.</p>
</text>
